.TH WIILAND-SHOW 1 "August 2026" "wiiland" "WiiLand Manual"
.SH NAME
wiiland-show \- inspect and exercise a connected Wii Remote
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wiiland-show --help
.br
.B wiiland-show list
.br
.B wiiland-show
.I positive-ordinal
.br
.B wiiland-show
.I /sys/path/to/device
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wiiland-show list
queries the running daemon for connected Wii Remotes and writes one tab-separated positive ordinal
and sysfs path per line.  It is intended for pipelines and does not require a
terminal.  An empty list is successful and produces no lines.
.PP
The ordinal and absolute-path forms observe one remote through daemon IPC in an interactive
ratatui/crossterm terminal interface.  The ordinal is resolved in daemon device
order, as printed by
.BR list .
The path form must begin with
.BR /sys/
\&.  A zero, malformed, overflowing, or otherwise non-positive ordinal is
rejected, as are extra arguments.
.PP
After opening the device and before checking terminal state, the program
prints:
.PP
.nf
Using Wii Remote: /sys/path/to/device
.fi
.PP
Interactive mode then requires a terminal on both standard input and standard
output, a non-empty TERM other than
.BR dumb ,
and at least 80 columns by 24 lines.  It enters raw mode and an alternate
screen.  The basic view is used when both dimensions meet the 80 by 24 minimum but either
dimension is below 160 columns or 48 lines.  The extended view is used only
when both dimensions are at least 160 by 48.  A smaller terminal is rejected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print help and exit successfully.  Help lists the interactive keyboard
commands.
.PP
.TP
.B --direct
Own hardware directly. Stop wiilandd before using this mode. Device listing
uses the hardware monitor, and all hardware commands below are available.
.TP
.B --socket PATH
Connect to an explicit daemon socket instead of the private per-user default.
This option conflicts with --direct. Device selection remains positional.
.PP
Daemon capture requires protocol 1.1 or newer and keeps normal virtual input
active. A daemon disconnect or capture queue overflow ends the session and
restores the terminal. Start a new session to reconnect.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
In daemon mode, q and f are available. The remaining hardware commands require
--direct. Commands are recognized on key press or repeat:
.TP
.B q
Quit and restore the terminal.
.TP
.B f
Freeze or unfreeze the displayed values.  Input events continue to be read,
but values are not updated while frozen.
.TP
.B s
Refresh static values such as battery, LED state, device type, and extension.
.TP
.B k
Toggle core key-event monitoring.
.TP
.B a
Toggle accelerometer monitoring.
.TP
.B i
Toggle infrared-camera monitoring.
.TP
.B m
Toggle MotionPlus monitoring.
.TP
.B n
Toggle MotionPlus normalization (50 when enabled, 0 when disabled).
.TP
.B N
Toggle Nunchuk monitoring.
.TP
.B c
Toggle Classic Controller monitoring.
.TP
.B b
Toggle Balance Board monitoring.
.TP
.B p
Toggle Wii U Pro Controller monitoring.
.TP
.B g
Toggle Guitar controller monitoring.
.TP
.B d
Toggle Drums controller monitoring.
.TP
.B r
Toggle the rumble motor when writable.  Read-only input reports rumble as
unavailable.
.TP
.B 1 , 2 , 3 , 4
Toggle the corresponding Wii Remote LED when writable.
.PP
The interface displays available controller data and button state, including
core accelerometer and IR values, MotionPlus, Nunchuk, Classic Controller,
Balance Board, Pro Controller, Guitar, and Drums values when those interfaces
are available.  Hotplug watch and device-gone events are reported in the
status area; readable interfaces remain usable when optional writable controls
cannot be opened.
.SH NON-INTERACTIVE USE
For redirected or piped output use
.BR "wiiland-show list" .
For an ordinal or path selection, the resolved-device line is printed before
terminal checks.  If standard input is not a terminal, the program then emits
an error that interactive UI requires a terminal on stdin; if standard output
is not a terminal, it emits the corresponding stdout error.  Empty or
.B dumb
TERM produces a usable-TERM error.  These checks return failure rather than
falling back to a non-interactive device dump.
.SH PERMISSIONS
Readable hid-wiimote input access is sufficient for monitoring.  Rumble and
LED controls require writable device access and are disabled when unavailable.
The program does not elevate privileges.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero for help, a successful device listing, or a normally closed
interactive session.  Returns one for invalid arguments, an unavailable or
unresolved device, monitor creation failure, insufficient input access,
non-TTY or unusable TERM, a terminal smaller than 80 by 24, or an interactive
runtime or terminal-restoration failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
List devices for a pipeline:
.PP
.nf
$ wiiland-show list
1	/sys/devices/platform/example/0005:057E:0306.0001
.fi
.PP
Open the first listed device:
.PP
.nf
$ wiiland-show 1
Using Wii Remote: /sys/devices/platform/example/0005:057E:0306.0001
.fi
.PP
Open the same device by path:
.PP
.nf
$ wiiland-show /sys/devices/platform/example/0005:057E:0306.0001
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wiilandd (1),
.BR wiiland-config (1),
.BR wiiland (7)
